#
# The controller's pins (its node's pin group: MISO, MOSI and SCLK on ALT0) and
# its chip selects (`cs-gpios`, plain outputs it drives around each
# transaction) go through the GPIO block; its key owns those pins only.
uses gpio_v1 via device compatible "brcm,bcm2835-gpio" or device compatible "brcm,bcm2711-gpio"
{
    set_function, set_level
}
# The controller divides the core clock (`clocks = <&clocks 20>`), which the
# firmware scales: the divisor is sized against its fastest rate.
uses mailbox_v1 via device compatible "raspberrypi,bcm2835-firmware", mboxes { get_max_clock_rate }
